[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/OperationArtemis/main/docs/steam/01-operation-artemis.jpg[/img]

[i]“If it goes wrong, listen to 108.0. At night. First the numbers, then the voice. — V.”[/i]
Found in the pocket of a dead soldier. Knox County, July 1993.

The evacuations never came. The emergency broadcast loops the same reassuring lies. But on a frequency nobody listens to anymore, someone is counting.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/OperationArtemis/main/docs/steam/02-follow-the-signal.jpg[/img]

They call themselves V. They worked inside the Zone, on the other side of the fence. They know where the army hid its records, and they are running out of time.

Wait for the dark. Turn the dial. Listen to the numbers.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/OperationArtemis/main/docs/steam/03-read-between-the-lines.jpg[/img]

A bunker beneath March Ridge. A clinic in West Point. A radio relay that still remembers V's voice, if you can bring the power back. Every document you recover answers one question and opens two more.

Why were soldiers waiting at the clinic door before the first patient ever arrived?
Why are the orders dated two days before anyone fell sick?

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/OperationArtemis/main/docs/steam/06-in-game-orders.jpg[/img]
[i]Real in-game document. Read the margins: someone was here before you.[/i]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/OperationArtemis/main/docs/steam/04-the-base-wakes-up.jpg[/img]

Deep underground, the answers are kept in a quiet room. Taking them is easy. Leaving with them is not. The moment the dossier crosses the gate, the alarms start, the red lights turn, and the base wakes up.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/OperationArtemis/main/docs/steam/05-get-out-alive.jpg[/img]

Three ways out of the Exclusion Zone. A helicopter at dawn. A ferryman on the river. A checkpoint on the bridge. Each one has its price, its own ending, and some may close before you reach them.

Survival was only the beginning.

[h2]WHAT AWAITS YOU[/h2]

[list]
[*]A mystery woven into your own survival run on the vanilla map: documents, a radio, a journal and your own decisions.
[*]Real places across Knox County, readable evidence, and a voice that talks to you.
[*]A laboratory escape, three exfiltration routes, a victory screen and voiced epilogues in English and French.
[*]An optional sterilization countdown that turns the Zone against you, plus sandbox settings for discovery, intensity and extraction timing.
[/list]

[h2]HOW IT BEGINS[/h2]

Enable Operation Artemis and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3811010882]Signal Smoke[/url]. Then survive. Search the soldiers who fell in the outbreak: one of them carries a notebook. Read it, find a radio, and wait for nightfall.

[h2]GOOD TO KNOW[/h2]

Project Zomboid Build 42.21. Tested in singleplayer; multiplayer and optional integrations still need their own validation. Story text in English, French, German, Spanish, Portuguese, Brazilian Portuguese, Russian, Turkish, Chinese, Japanese and Korean (in Chinese, Japanese and Korean the in-game documents stay in English). Voiced endings in English and French.

[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3817018338][b]Belt Walkie-Talkie[/b][/url] (optional) is recommended: one shared belt walkie-talkie behaviour for all the mods that use it. Without it, the same behaviour is built in.

[h2]SUPPORT THE PROJECT[/h2]

Enjoy the scenario? A coffee helps fund the next stories and updates.

